# ─── DRAM simulation data (large datasets) ─────────────────────────
# Untracked wholesale by default (large generated/binary data, not
# source). MLP student-handout fixtures are the one exception, but only
# their directory structure + small non-binary metadata (config.json) is
# tracked -- manifest.json (mlp_bin/, auto-generated from the .pth's real
# tensor shapes at dump time) and every .bin/.pth/.zip (tensors, weight
# checkpoints, the packaged archive) stay untracked regardless of which
# directory they're in (large/regenerable, or -- for manifest.json --
# derived output that's meant to be regenerated by mlp_weight_writer.py,
# not hand-diffed in git). Directory negations must precede their own file
# negations (git requires the parent directory to be un-ignored before
# a file inside it can be).
new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/*
!new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/model_weight/
!new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/model_weight/5mlp_weight/
!new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/model_weight/5mlp_weight/**/
new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/model_weight/5mlp_weight/**/*.bin
new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/model_weight/5mlp_weight/**/*.pth
new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/model_weight/5mlp_weight/**/*.zip
!new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/model_weight/mlp_bin/
!new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/model_weight/mlp_bin/**/
new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/model_weight/mlp_bin/**/*.bin
new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/model_weight/mlp_bin/**/manifest.json
# test_dram: hand-crafted small binary fixtures for test_dram/test_dram_
# address_mapper -- was previously tracked directly (predates the blanket
# DRAM_data/ ignore above); explicitly untracked here going forward.
new_code/DRAM_sim/DRAM_data/test_dram/

